== Trivia ==
* {{e|Death's Head}}, {{e|Flesh Death's Head}}, Stonies, Cross Stonies, and {{e|Eggy|text=Eggies}} are the only non-boss enemies with a death animation.
* Conjoined Fatties and Bloaties are one of five enemies (four without ''Repentance'', three without ''Afterbirth+'') in the game that use [[Creep]] as projectiles, the others are {{e|Ultra Pride}}, {{e|Meatball}}s and {{e|The Thing}}.
* Blubbers appear to be headless Pale Fatties or, more accurately, headless Fat Sacks.
** Similarly, Half Sacks appear to be the lower portions of Pale Fatties or, more accurately, the lower portions of Fat Sacks.
* {{dlc|a}} Conjoined Fatties and Blue Conjoined Fatties suffer the condition of [[wikipedia:Polycephaly|polycephaly]], having more than one head.
* {{dlc|ana+}} Conjoined Fatties and Blue Conjoined Fatties make the same high-pitched growling noises as {{e|Gaper}}s instead of the lower-pitched ones used by other Fatties.
* {{dlc|a+}} Stoneys make the sounds of a pitched-down Gaper.
** {{dlc|r}} Stoneys make the sounds of a pitched-down Fatty.
* {{dlc|a+}} Antibirth developer Kilburn first revealed Cross Stoneys on the 1st of April for Booster Pack #5.<ref>[https://twitter.com/FixItVinh/status/980490518747631616 ''"Looking good."'']</ref>
** It was revealed on the 1st of April, and Cross Stoneys are exclusive to the Aprils Fool Challenge.
* {{dlc|r}} [[Anti:Bubbles|Bubbles]], [[Anti:Quakey|Quakies]], and [[Anti:Big Bony|Big Bonies]] originate from the ''Antibirth'' mod.
** In ''Antibirth'', Quakies have a different face.
** The Big Bony's bone attack is also different from ''Antibirth'', where the bone was instead a lobbed projectile that created shockwaves in the place of its impact. Big Bonies also used to spawn in {{s|Mausoleum|n}}.
* {{dlc|r}} Vis Fatties look very similar to {{e|Exorcist|n}}s.
* {{dlc|r}} Bloaty's name and design is somewhat a reminiscent to the human corpse's bloating stage, which causes the corpse to swell up and bear swollen lips and eyeballs due to gas.
* {{dlc|r}} Shadies are inspired by the Shadow Ninja enemy from the ''Shadow Warrior'' game series.<ref>https://ibb.co/dtzb7Zy</ref>

